    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "q-32246: eliminating x gives (4−3k)y=0. Infinitely many solutions require 4−3k=0, hence k=4/3. q-32245: elimination gives (k+2)y=−2, which is inconsistent exactly when k=−2. q-32026: the coefficient determinant is 31; the selected inverse matrix product gives (x,y)=(3/31,−8/31). q-102705: the coefficient determinant is 2; the selected product gives (x,y)=(1/2,1). In both matrix choices, the source uses x to denote the solution vector. Each answer agrees with its own captured worked solution. The two previously reviewed matrix answers remain confirmed; no submitted grade was supplied.",
